tr_by=hand
why=pelt#49, ruling #113, pelt#42: with set -o autocd and a command_not_found_handle defined (lope's shape: a fuzzy word it jumps for, 127 for the rest), a name with no slash that names a directory goes to cd and the handler is not called; a name that is no directory goes to the handler as sh21 built it (its status the command's, a 127 said as not found); a slashed directory goes to cd. bash 5.3 agrees on the order (black-box, notes/sh23-evidence/refs/base/bash-i-autocd/p07-hook); its handler runs in a subshell, pelt's in the shell. Written by hand from pelt trunk's answers to the explicit session (notes/sh23-evidence/handtr.py)
